          lemma: "πέντε ἄρτους κριθίνους",
          title: "Five barley loaves",
          body: "**Barley** was the grain of the poor — coarse, cheap bread, and a small child’s packed lunch at that. John notes it deliberately: the abundance will come from almost nothing, given into Jesus’ hands. The scene also rhymes with **Elisha**, who fed a hundred men from twenty barley loaves and had some left over (2 Kings 4:42–44); here the prophet greater than Elisha feeds thousands from five, with twelve baskets to spare.",
