      annotations: [
        {
          id: 'a6.27.1',
          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g6.27.6', 'g6.27.11'],
          lemma: "βρῶσιν … τὴν μένουσαν",
          title: "Food that perishes, food that lasts",
          body: "Yesterday’s loaves are already gone; that is the nature of **food that perishes** — you eat, and hunger returns (as at the well, 4:13). Jesus redirects all that daily striving toward **food that endures to eternal life**, which — the twist — is not *earned* but *given*: “which the Son of Man **will give** you.” You work *for* it only in the sense of the next verses: the one work is to receive him. To “labour” for this bread is to stop labouring and take the gift.",
        },
      ],
