      annotations: [
        {
          id: 'a6.37.1',
          kind: "concept",
          refs: ['g6.37.3', 'g6.37.17'],
          lemma: "οὐ μὴ ἐκβάλω ἔξω",
          title: "“I will never cast out”",
          body: "Against the grumbling and unbelief, a rock of assurance. Two truths hold together: the Father **gives** a people to the Son, and *all of them* **will come**; and everyone who actually comes finds not a wary gatekeeper but an unbreakable welcome — **“I will never cast out.”** The double negative in Greek (**οὐ μὴ**) is the strongest possible: *never, no never.* The verses that follow spell out why it is unbreakable — the Son’s whole mission is to **lose nothing** the Father has given and to raise it up at the last day (vv. 38–40). Coming is your part; keeping is his.",
        },
      ],
